    "title": "MercyOne Siouxland lawsuit moves to be dismissed - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Reilly Mahon Maren Ewertz ,\n1 hours ago\nSIOUX CITY , Iowa ( KCAU ) — A lawsuit against the former MercyOne Siouxland Medical Center is moving forward to being dismissed.\nCourt documents indicate that Cynthia Tener filed for dismissal with prejudice in District Court on September 9. A judge still needs to rule whether or not the suit will be dismissed.\nJudge finds that Board of Medicine withheld information from accused doctor Tener filed the wrongful termination lawsuit in 2022, accusing MercyOne and its affiliated companies of firing her . This was due to reporting public safety concerns and malpractice concerns involving a heart surgeon to MercyOne’s ethics committee.\nEarlier in September, UnityPoint Health acquired MercyOne Siouxland , with the transition of ownership complete.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to SiouxlandProud | Sioux City, IA | News, Weather, and Sports.",
